<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
    Gesher's system font configuration, installed as $ANDROID_ROOT/etc/fonts.xml
    with the font files in $ANDROID_ROOT/fonts (docs/fonts.md).

    A subset of AOSP's frameworks/base/data/fonts/fonts.xml at android-16.0.0_r4
    (Apache License 2.0): the families whose fonts Gesher ships, unchanged.
      sans-serif (+ condensed)  Roboto-Regular.ttf, Roboto 3.011 variable (wght, wdth, ital)
      serif                     NotoSerif-{Regular,Bold,Italic,BoldItalic}.ttf
      monospace                 DroidSansMono.ttf
      fallback und-Arab         Noto Naskh Arabic 1.070 (elegant) and Noto Naskh
                                Arabic UI (compact), regular and bold
      fallback und-Hebr         NotoSansHebrew-{Regular,Bold}.ttf (1.040)
      fallback und-Thai         Noto Sans Thai and Noto Sans Thai UI, regular and bold
      fallback und-Deva         Noto Sans Devanagari 2.006 and Noto Sans Devanagari
                                UI, variable (wght)
    Serif fallbacks (fallbackFor="serif") are left out of these families.
    Left out: the other families and the other scripts' fallbacks,
    serif-monospace, casual, cursive, smallcaps, source-sans-pro, roboto-flex.
    CJK, emoji, symbols and the other scripts come from the fonts Windows
    has, in place: windows-fonts.xml, appended to this file's fallback list
    (docs/fonts.md, docs/decisions/0044-rtl-scripts-and-locale.md).
    In this file, all fonts without names are added to the default list.
-->
